# The canon is all clear sky, so it only ever shows the web a sun that casts. An
# overcast takes the sun's shadow away (WeatherLook.OVERCAST over 0.6), and on
# Compatibility that is a different pass with its own count-back (CompatTrim's
# OPEN rows). These are the frames that fit and prove them, desktop and web alike:
#   tools/tour.sh tours/degrade_grey.tour --seed=7
#   tools/web.sh --no-export --quick --tour=tours/degrade_grey.tour --args=--seed=7
weather grey:1
place spawn
hour 12
wait 0.8
shot g1-spawn-grey-noon with land:coast
place moss
wait 0.8
shot g2-moss-grey with land:moss
place snowfield
wait 0.8
shot g3-snowfield-grey with land:snowfield
place spawn
hour 23
wait 0.8
shot g4-spawn-grey-night
tap lamp
wait 0.4
shot g5-grey-night-lamp with lamp
